WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.781 --> 00:00:09.144
Interests are topics you follow. Each one looks for new things on its own schedule, delivers what it found when you choose, and learns from your ratings.

2
00:00:09.848 --> 00:00:17.315
Open Interests in the sidebar. Each interest shows its schedule, its last run, what waits for delivery, and your ratings.

3
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:26.071
To follow a new topic, choose New interest. Give it a name, and describe the angle you want. The agents follow the description first.

4
00:00:26.771 --> 00:00:35.710
The run schedule is when it looks. The delivery schedule is when you hear about it: as one digest at set times, or as soon as a run finishes.

5
00:00:36.409 --> 00:00:39.502
Add a taste rule if you like, then choose Create interest.

6
00:00:41.646 --> 00:00:46.083
The Taste tab keeps your explicit rules. They win over what your ratings suggest.

7
00:00:46.784 --> 00:00:56.021
Back on the list, the daily quiet cap limits how many digest items all interests together put on your desk in a day. Owners and Admins can change it.

8
00:00:56.733 --> 00:01:04.968
This interest found three items that wait for its next delivery time. Deliver 3 now puts them on your desk straight away, within the quiet cap.

9
00:01:05.668 --> 00:01:08.463
They show up in the Digest tab, where you rate them.

10
00:01:09.164 --> 00:01:16.289
An interest you no longer need is archived from More actions. It stops running and leaves the list, but nothing is lost.

11
00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:20.659
Tick Show archived to find it again, open it, and choose Restore.

12
00:01:23.402 --> 00:01:28.693
That is Interests: follow a topic, choose when you hear about it, and let your ratings sharpen it.
